    Close the lookup binding matrix and wire the production plan (partial progress)
    
    The hidden fixture proximity code is sized for the full digit-set multiplicity message, and the lookup plan is built by the parent-plan constructor from the trusted rounding layout and the parent codes instead of hand-picked sources. The binding matrix adds first-message root, sample and opening tampering, a missing second-stage lookup carrier, a changed committed digit, duplicate and multi-message key sources, and a d=1 zero-range digit check; the verifier-visible proof is checked not to carry the private key vector.
    
    The rounding claim and the model-level plan assembly are not part of this step.

